sentences.l:
And the two of them in turn, in the hut, Odysseus and the heavenly swineherd,
were making ready breakfast with the dawn, having kindled a fire,
and sent out the herdsmen with the gathered swine;

“Eumaeus, truly some companion of yours will come here,
or else another acquaintance, since the dogs do not bark,
but fawn all round;

And he went to meet his lord,
and kissed him, head and both fine eyes
and both hands;

From broad Crete his birth he declares,
and says over many cities of mortals to have been whirled about,
straying;

at once then from me my head let cut off a foreign man,
if I were not to all of them an evil,
having gone to the hall of Laertes’ son Odysseus.
